{% set listedNpcs = whileYouWereAwayNpcs or [] %}
<task>Resolve what changed while the player was away, then write return prose from the player's perspective.</task>

{% for npc in listedNpcs %}For {{ npc.name }} (last seen {{ npc.lastSeenTimeAgo }} at {{ npc.lastSeenLocationName | default(npc.last_seen_location, true) }}), return exactly one complete <characterUpdate> XML block using this exact schema. Do not include another character or substitute field names:
<characterUpdate>
  <name>{{ npc.name }}</name>
  <needBarChanges>
    <needBarEffect><needBarId>configured need-bar id</needBarId><value>current value from 0 to 100%, or N/A</value></needBarEffect>
  </needBarChanges>
  <travelDestination><location>exact location if they left</location><region>exact region if they left</region></travelDestination>
  <update>Concise hidden summary of what they did while the player was away.</update>
</characterUpdate>
Use one <needBarEffect> per applicable need bar; leave <needBarChanges> empty if none apply. Omit <travelDestination> when they stayed here. The <update> field is always required.

{% llmparse('while_away_character_update', npc.name) %}
{% endfor %}

Identify only exact-location arrivals not already listed and not in the party. Return one <characterUpdates> XML block; leave it empty when there are none. Do not place merely nearby characters here. Every arrival must use the same canonical <characterUpdate> schema above, with the exact existing character name, <needBarChanges>, literal <travelDestination>HERE</travelDestination>, and required <update>.

{% llmparse('while_away_arrival_updates') %}

Identify only existing items/scenery that moved with the player or party from the previous location. Return one <itemSceneryMoves> XML block containing exact <itemName> values; leave it empty when none moved.

{% llmparse('exact_xml_root', 'itemSceneryMoves', { allowEmptyRoot: true }) %}

Plan what the player can directly see, learn, or experience on return. Do not expose the hidden character updates as omniscient narration.

{% llm_dummy_action %}

Draft Response: Write a few return-scene paragraphs from the player's perspective. Always provide prose, even when no character update exists. Output prose only.

{% llm_dummy_action %}

{% set tinyBrainAuditFocus = 'Player-facing prose must not expose hidden/offscreen knowledge; exact-location arrivals must not include nearby or party characters; structured changes must not contradict the staged update blocks.' %}
{% include "_includes/tinybrain-prose-audit.njk" %}

Reproduce the previously approved characterUpdate blocks without changing them. Insert the <characterUpdate> children from the approved arrival <characterUpdates> block directly into the single outer <characterUpdates>; do not nest a second <characterUpdates> wrapper. Reproduce the approved itemSceneryMoves contents without changing them, and add the polished prose. Return XML only:
<response><proseForPlayer>polished return prose</proseForPlayer><characterUpdates>all approved character updates and arrivals</characterUpdates><itemSceneryMoves>all approved item/scenery names</itemSceneryMoves></response>
